Release Notes unified i.MX 6UL/ULL Linux BSP:
=============================================

BSP-Yocto-Ampliphy-i.MX6UL-PD24.1.0             2024-07-19
==========================================================
- Linux Mainline Kernel v6.6.31 (LTS kernel)
  * Update from v5.15.102 to v6.6.31
  * Tag: v6.6.31-phy2
- barebox v2024.03.0
  * Tag: v2024.03.0-phy1
- Yocto 5.0.2 (scarthgap)
- Qt 5.15.13 from meta-qt5 (scarthgap)

Supported Images/Machines:
--------------------------
- phytec-headless-image on:
  * phyboard-segin-imx6ul-2
  * phyboard-segin-imx6ul-6
  * phyboard-segin-imx6ul-7
  * phyboard-segin-imx6ul-8
  * phygate-tauri-s-imx6ul-1

- phytec-qt5demo-image on:
  * phyboard-segin-imx6ul-2
  * phyboard-segin-imx6ul-6
  * phyboard-segin-imx6ul-7
  * phyboard-segin-imx6ul-8

- phytec-vision-image on:
  * phyboard-segin-imx6ul-6
  * phyboard-segin-imx6ul-7

- phytec-securiphy-image on:
  * phyboard-segin-imx6ul-6
  * phyboard-segin-imx6ul-8
  * phygate-tauri-s-imx6ul-1

Note: For decoding Machine Names into hardware ordering please visit our download area and use the machine decoder there.
https://www.phytec.de/bsp-download/?bsp=BSP-Yocto-Ampliphy-i.MX6UL-PD24.1.0

Build Environment:
------------------
- Ubuntu 22.04 64Bit


Known Issues:
-------------
- kernel:
  * Small performance drop on IO-operations with external devices when
    LOW-POWER-IDLE state is active (CONFIG_CPUIDLE)
- phyGATE-Tauri-S RS232 / RS485:
  * At the same time only '2x RS232' or '1x RS232 and 1x RS485' can be used on
    phyGATE-Tauri-S. Right now '1x RS232 and 1x RS485' is the default.
- PEB-WLBT-05-15x modules (5 GHz option) don't work. They are using Sterling-LWB5 chips,
  which is EOL.

Notes:
------
- 'phytec-security-image' is renamed to 'phytec-securiphy-image'.
- 'security' distro is renamed to 'securiphy'.
- .wic image support is dropped. Users should use .partup image format with partup
  tool for SD-Card/eMMC update.

- For a list of changes in former releases, please read release note of PD22.1.1
